 [1C- [1mThe note under the list:[22m the "E[1Ctimated at…"[1Cnote[1Cis[1Cgone.[1CThe[1Conly[1Cline[1Cleft[1Cis[1C"Timetable[1Cdata[1Cfrom[1C{date}[1Cmay[1Cbe[1Cout[1Cof[1Cdate.",[1Cshown[1Conly[1Cwhen[1Cthe[1Ctimetable[1Cis[1Cmore[1Cthan[1C24    hours old, and in the minim[1Cs[1Cd[1Csheet[1Ctoo.[34;3H-[1m[1CNew section, "Minimising the phone sheet":[22m[K[35;5H- You can tap the handle, which is now a real "Minimise"/"Expand" button, or swipe at least 40 px down or[1Cup.[36;5H- Why the swipe doesn't use pointer capture, and why the phone sheet has [38;2;177;185;249mtouch-action: none[m.                                                                                    [37;5H- A table of what each sheet state keeps when minimised. In the nearest-stop state the one bus row carries its own Scheduled badge, so an estimate is always labelled.[K[38;5H- The minimised state isn't saved, and minimising never moves the map.[K[39;3H-[1m[1CMap section:[22m the line saying the header badge is the only visible "Scheduled" label now also mentions the badge in the minimised row.[K[40;6H[K[41;3HWhere the plan and the code differed, I followed the code. The main difference is the swipe: the plan put[1Cthe[1Crelease[1Chandler[1Con[1Cthe[1Csheet[1Citself,[1Cbut[1Cthe[1Ccode[1Clistens[1Con[1Cthe[42;3Hwindow, so a mouse released outside the sheet still counts.[38;2;233;154;122m[44;3HHerding…[38;2;153;153;153m[2Crunning Stop[1Ch[1Cok ·[1C56s · ↓ 4.2k tokens · thought for 6s)[47;3H[?25h[?25l[m[38;2;215;119;87m[44;1H✽[38;2;228;144;112m[1CHerding…[47;3H[?25h[m]0;✳ 006 sheet improvements[?25l[38;2;153;153;153m[44;1H✻[1CWorked for 56s · done 10:40[1CAM[K[m[47;1H❯ [?25h[?25l[2mshow me the diff of map-screen.md[47;3H[?25h[22m